Merkur vendors modified copies of six third-party crates under
packages/*-patch. Each keeps the upstream license files it was published with
and records Merkur's modification in its README.

The lint rules under tools/biome/slop restate the rules of the anti-slop
Oxlint plugin (https://github.com/dmmulroy/anti-slop, MIT, commit
c44ef22ca116d0ba62a3ff663a0bd13a3f3fa40b) as Biome GritQL plugins, and
tools/biome/slop/cases.json is taken from its tests.
tools/biome/slop/LICENSE-anti-slop holds its license. They are development
tools; no shipped artifact contains them.

The daemon carries the attribution and license text for every dependency
compiled into it; `merkur licenses` prints it.

